  "title": "TLS: recognize ech_required alert",
  "description": "This merge request is a tiny follow-up to https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/12260, which added dissector support for TLS Encrypted Client Hello (ECH).\n\n## Description\n\nThe [draft-ietf-tls-esni-17 document](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-tls-esni-17) defines an update to the IANA TLS\nalert registry in [Section 11.2](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-tls-esni-17#section-11.2):\n\n> IANA is requested to create an entry, ech_required(121) in the\n> existing registry for Alerts (defined in [RFC8446]), with the \"DTLS-OK\"\n> column set to \"Y\".\n\nThis branch updates the existing `ssl_31_alert_description` array to recognize alert 121 as \"ECH Required\".\n\n## Manual testing\n\nBefore applying this patch a pcap of a session where a client's ECH offer wasn't accepted by the server (following the logic in [§ 6.1.6](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-tls-esni-17#section-6.1.6)) results in the following unknown alert:\n\n```\nTLSv1.3 Record Layer: Alert (Level: Fatal, Description: Unknown)\n    Opaque Type: Application Data (23)\n    Version: TLS 1.2 (0x0303)\n    Length: 19\n    [Content Type: Alert (21)]\n    Alert Message\n        Level: Fatal (2)\n        Description: Unknown (121)\n```\n\nAfterwards, it is correctly identified as `ech_required`:\n\n```\nTLSv1.3 Record Layer: Alert (Level: Fatal, Description: ECH Required)\n    Opaque Type: Application Data (23)\n    Version: TLS 1.2 (0x0303)\n    Length: 19\n    [Content Type: Alert (21)]\n    Alert Message\n        Level: Fatal (2)\n        Description: ECH Required (121)\n```",
  "state": "merged",
